{{--
    The root view every Inertia response renders into.

    PUBLISHED BY `panel:install` AND YOURS TO EDIT. It is here because a fresh
    application has none, and without one the first panel route answers with
    "View [app] not found" - an error about a file nobody told you to write.

    DEFAULT PATH: published kit CSS/JS at public/vendor/panel. That is why
    `panel:install` after Composer is not a white page. `@vite` is used only
    when you have run `npm run build` and a Vite manifest exists.

    NO `@routes` DIRECTIVE. Ziggy and Wayfinder are both fine and neither is
    required: the packaged screens are given the URLs they need as props, so a
    route helper missing on the client is not a screen that breaks. Add one if
    your own pages want it.

    Appearance FOUC: keep `@include('panel::appearance-prepaint')` in <head>
    BEFORE any stylesheet or kit/Vite script. That include embeds the account
    JSON, critical #pk-appearance CSS, and a blocking setProperty script.
    See docs/01-install.md (Appearance FOUC contract).
--}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ str_replace('_', '-', app()->getLocale()) }}">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

        @include('panel::appearance-prepaint')

        <title inertia>{{ config('app.name', 'Panel') }}</title>

        @if (\Alxtexh\Panel\Support\KitAssets::hostViteManifestExists())
            @vite(['resources/js/app.ts'])
        @else
            @php(\Alxtexh\Panel\Support\KitAssets::publishIfMissing())
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('vendor/panel/app.css') }}">
            <script type="module" src="{{ asset('vendor/panel/app.js') }}"></script>
        @endif
        @inertiaHead
    </head>

    <body class="font-sans antialiased">
        @inertia
    </body>
</html>
